Changelog: 19-11-2026 22:12:37

Fixed. The message about a newer build says it comes once it has been tried on the board, not the console (owner, 19-11-2026: board everywhere).

Changelog: 18-11-2026 04:15:16

Release 1.3.0.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 03:30:14

Added. The controller's state beside the title, as the other managers show it: Controller connected, or No
controller when none is, looked at again every few seconds.

Changelog: 18-11-2026 03:22:15

Added. The managers' new design, as the other managers': Play time, a pill in the row of action pills, with the
time spent in all games together as Vita3K counts it. A Memory cards tab with the saves Vita3K keeps, each under
its game's title (export to a .zip, import, delete). Clear logs, a tab beside Log that is a button, empties the
app's log file and the Log tab and removes the older log files. Start game stands beside Your games. The six tabs
share the window's whole width and are pills as the ones above them. Under the header's pills only the links to
Vita3K's release notes and the wiki are left, in the type of a pill's caption; the introduction went. Vita3K's
state is one line, and so is the firmware's (Installed., Partly installed. or Not installed., each part in its
tooltip); the Firmware box in the header went. Under the games an info symbol stands in for the line of text
about Steam. The window opens 900 wide (it was 980), which is its narrowest, and 606 high (it was 800); the
Settings tab scrolls when it is higher than the window.

